Package: tree-sitter-cli
Version: __VERSION__
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: __ARCH__
Maintainer: Fernando Silveira <fsilveira@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter/
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libgcc-s1
Installed-Size: __INSTALLED_SIZE__
Description: command-line tool for Tree-sitter parsers
 Tree-sitter is a parser generator tool and an incremental parsing
 library. It can build a concrete syntax tree for a source file and
 efficiently update that tree as the source file is edited.
 .
 This package provides the tree-sitter-cli program, which is used to
 generate, build, and test Tree-sitter parsers.
 .
 This build repackages the official prebuilt binary published upstream
 at https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/releases. It is not
 built from source and is not affiliated with the Debian or Ubuntu
 tree-sitter-cli package maintainers.
